From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 07:30:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(control): copy-on-select follows the profile

CopyOnSelect() returned a hard false, so a ghostty pane ignored the setting
while a cascadia pane in the same window honoured it. The value is only ever
read back through LeftClickOnTerminal, so nothing else would have shown it up.

The out-param it feeds was wrong for a second reason: cascadia sets it to mean
"there is now a selection worth copying when the button comes up", not "copy on
select is enabled". A single click clears the selection and sets it false; a
double or triple click makes one and sets it true. A drag makes one too, and
now says so from SetSelectionAnchor, which is where a drag's selection begins -
the click that started the drag had nothing to copy yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BgDGqEqRBB8L5Ueoq1uuxy
---
 .../TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp    | 21 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
index 37bb4820a..833f2e6a8 100644
--- a/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
+++ b/src/cascadia/TerminalControl/GhosttyControlCore.cpp
@@ -942,6 +942,11 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         _mouseTo(positionCore);
         ghostty_surface_mouse_button(_surface, GHOSTTY_MOUSE_PRESS, GHOSTTY_MOUSE_LEFT, GHOSTTY_MODS_NONE);
         _mouseDown = true;
+
+        // A drag is about to make a selection, and ControlInteractivity decides
+        // whether to copy it on release from this event - the click that began
+        // the drag had nothing to copy yet and said so.
+        UpdateSelectionMarkers.raise(*this, winrt::make<implementation::UpdateSelectionMarkersEventArgs>(false));
     }
 
     void GhosttyControlCore::SetEndSelectionPoint(const Core::Point positionCore)
@@ -994,7 +999,15 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
         }
 
         _renderNow();
-        selectionNeedsToBeCopied = CopyOnSelect();
+
+        // Cascadia's meaning, not "is copy-on-select on": the flag says whether
+        // there is now a selection worth copying when the button comes up. A
+        // single click cleared one, so there is nothing; a double or triple
+        // click just made one.
+        //
+        // A drag makes one too, and says so from SetSelectionAnchor - the
+        // release that would copy it comes long after this call.
+        selectionNeedsToBeCopied = numberOfClicks > 1;
     }
 
     bool GhosttyControlCore::HasSelection() const
@@ -1153,7 +1166,11 @@ namespace winrt::Microsoft::Terminal::Control::implementation
     // history surface are Phase 6 (interaction parity). Each returns the
     // "nothing here" answer its caller already handles for an empty terminal,
     // so the shell degrades to a pane you can type in rather than misbehaving.
-    bool GhosttyControlCore::CopyOnSelect() const { return false; }
+    // The profile's setting, not a constant. Returning false here meant a
+    // ghostty pane silently ignored copyOnSelect while a cascadia pane in the
+    // same window honoured it - and the value is only ever read back out
+    // through LeftClickOnTerminal, so nothing else would have shown it up.
+    bool GhosttyControlCore::CopyOnSelect() const { return _settings && _settings.CopyOnSelect(); }
     bool GhosttyControlCore::ToggleBlockSelection() { return false; }
     void GhosttyControlCore::ToggleMarkMode() {}
     Control::SelectionInteractionMode GhosttyControlCore::SelectionMode() const { return Control::SelectionInteractionMode::None; }
